          "markdown": "**Scenario: Meteorological Station**\n1. Calculate the 25th and 75th percentiles (IQR) for numerical values.\n2. Clip extreme values to `[Q1 - 1.5*IQR, Q3 + 1.5*IQR]` using `np.clip`.\n3. Compute standard z-score normalization `(x - mean) / std`.",
          "code": "import numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\ndata = {'day': [1, 2, 3, 4, 5], 'wind_speed': [10.0, 15.0, np.nan, 25.0, 12.0], 'rainfall': [0.0, 5.0, 10.0, 0.0, 2.5]}\ndf = pd.DataFrame(data)\n\n# --------------------------------------------------\n# TODO: IQR clipping and Z-score normalization\n# --------------------------------------------------\n",
          "solution": "import numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\ndata = {'day': [1, 2, 3, 4, 5], 'wind_speed': [10.0, 15.0, np.nan, 25.0, 12.0], 'rainfall': [0.0, 5.0, 10.0, 0.0, 2.5]}\ndf = pd.DataFrame(data)\nnum_col = df.columns[1]\nvals = df[num_col].dropna()\nq1, q3 = vals.quantile(0.25), vals.quantile(0.75)\niqr = q3 - q1\nclipped = np.clip(vals, q1 - 1.5 * iqr, q3 + 1.5 * iqr)\nz_score = (clipped - clipped.mean()) / clipped.std()\nprint('Z-Score Output:')\nprint(z_score)\n",
